# round 109 (w126): does the module help a backbone with NO curated pathway annotation? Every cell of rounds 75 to 107 reads the pathway multi-hot beside ProtT5, which a new dataset may not have. These arms drop it: ProtT5 alone with the single-experiment module (the YPD growth ratio, the YPD flux vector and the six gene-rule counts) against ProtT5 alone with nothing on the logit, on the ten repeated outer splits, three seeds each. Read fixed here: the per-split seed-mean paired difference, mean, standard deviation and sign count over ten splits, against the +0.061 the same module is worth on the pathway backbone (w104 against w94 pathpool). No p-value; the test blocks overlap.
